mbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy","abstract":[{"text":"OpenID Connect surface controls (X7 G8, plan §4.6\/§4.8; T21.4). Settings that are not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"password rules, here because this is the org-baseline-plus-tenant-override surface every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other per-tenant control lives on. They are not all of the same kind as each other, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which is which is the whole of what [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"validate_tenant_override"},{"text":"] and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clamp_overrides_to_org"},{"text":"] read, so it is set out rather than inferred. ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Ordered","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tenant may be stricter than its organization and never more permissive: *"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::sensitive_scopes_enabled"},{"text":"], validated ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"disable-only","type":"text"}]},{"text":" — the mirror image of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mfa_enforced"},{"text":", because releasing personal data is the less-restrictive direction, so a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tenant can turn its organization’s decision off but never on. * [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::saml_idp_enabled"},{"text":"],","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"validated ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"disable-only","type":"text"}]},{"text":" exactly like [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::sensitive_scopes_enabled"},{"text":"] (D-20): a tenant","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"may turn its organization’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"text":" off and never its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"text":" on. * [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::ssf_enabled"},{"text":"],","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"validated ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"disable-only","type":"text"}]},{"text":" the same way (D-45). * [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::dynamic_registration"},{"text":"], on the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ladder ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"disabled"},{"text":" → ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"initial_access_token"},{"text":" → ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"anonymous"},{"text":": a tenant may move down it and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"never up. * [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::dcr_max_clients"},{"text":"] and [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::dcr_unused_client_ttl_days"},{"text":"], on the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ordinary ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tenant <= org"},{"text":" rule — with the wrinkle that ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0"},{"text":" on the second means ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"never sweep"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which is the longest window of all and is handled by [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dcr_ttl_strictness"},{"text":"]. ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ordered","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":", therefore never validated against the baseline and never clamped: *","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::default_locale"},{"text":"]. A language is a presentation preference; there is no sense in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which Italian is stricter than French. * [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::dcr_allowed_scopes"},{"text":"],","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::dcr_allowed_redirect_hosts"},{"text":"] and [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::external_client_allowed_resources"},{"text":"]. Each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"names per-tenant resources — ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"this","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" tenant’s MCP servers, ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"this"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" tenant’s callback hosts —","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and there is no sense in which one such list is stricter than another. A subset rule would","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"force an organization to enumerate every tenant’s resource servers in its own baseline","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"before any tenant could name one. The model’s rule is “a tenant may only be more","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"restrictive”, which binds every field that ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"has"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" a restrictiveness; a field that has none","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"cannot violate it. One cross-field interlock spans both groups and is checked on the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"resolved policy rather than on either input: see [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"validate_dcr_policy"},{"text":"].","type":"text"}],"title":"OidcPolicy","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The official Swift SDK for AXIAM (Access eXtended Identity and Authorization Management)."}],"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk","kind":"symbol","title":"AxiamSDK","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"}}}